body:
> I believe fullscreen spec is broken indeed and [whatwg/fullscreen#15](https://github.com/whatwg/fullscreen/issues/15) should be fixed. The problem is that while it is broken and if this PR is added on top of the brokenness, things are even more broken.

I see what you mean. I agree the spec issue you link should be fixed. Anyways, this particular fullscreen case could be handled somewhere in the `allow focus steps` to not make things worse, probably adding another step so the algorithm looks like follows:

``` 
algorithm allow_focus(focus_setter_frame, target_frame, currently_focused_frame):
  if target_frame has transient user activation:
    return true

  if focus_setter_frame has the policy allowed:
    return true

  // New step added for fullscreen.
  if currently_focused_frame's fullscreen flag is set to true:
    return false

  // New step added with this proposal.
  if currently_focused_frame is an inclusive descendant frame of focus_setter_frame:
    return true

  return false
```

`currently_focused_frame's fullscreen flag` refers to https://fullscreen.spec.whatwg.org/#iframe-fullscreen-flag

Just to recap, this is the scenario you brought up:

A hosts B hosts C, policy denied in B and C, C is in fullscreen and focused, transient user activation expired, B calls focus on an element of itself.

With the algorithm above, B wouldn't be allowed to do that.
